n_to=%2Fnodejs%2FRelease)You must be signed in to change notification settings\n- [Fork682 (682)](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fnodejs%2FRelease)\n- [Star4.4k (4.4k)](https://github.com/login?return_to=%2Fnodejs%2FRelease)You must be signed in to star a repository\n\n## About\n\nNode.js Release Working Group\n\n### Topics\n\n[node](https://github.com/topics/node)[nodejs](https://github.com/topics/nodejs)\n\n### Resources\n\n[Readme](#readme-ov-file)\n\n### Code of conduct\n\n[Code of conduct](https://github.com/nodejs/release#coc-ov-file)\n\n### Contributing\n\n[Contributing](#contributing-ov-file)\n\n### Security policy\n\n[Security policy](#security-ov-file)\n\n[Activity](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/activity)\n\n[Custom properties](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/custom-properties)\n\n### Stars\n\n**4.4k** stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n**313** watching\n\n### Forks\n\n[**682** forks](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/forks)\n\n[Report repository](https://github.com/contact/report-content?content_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fnodejs%2FRelease&report=nodejs%20%28user%29)\n\nmain\n\n[Branches](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/branches)[Tags](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/tags)\n\n[/nodejs/Release/branches](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/branches)[/nodejs/Release/tags](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/tags)\n\nGo to file\n\nCode\n\nOpen more actions menu\n\n## Latest commit\n\n \n\n## History\n\n[352 Commits](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/commits/main/)\n\n[/nodejs/Release/commits/main/](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/commits/main/)352 Commits\n\n## Folders and files\n\n| Name                                                                                                                     |   | Name                                                                                                                     | Last commit message | Last commit date |\n|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|------------------|\n| [doc](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/tree/main/doc \"doc\")                                                             |   | [doc](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/tree/main/doc \"doc\")                                                             |                     |                  |\n| [.editorconfig](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/.editorconfig \".editorconfig\")                               |   | [.editorconfig](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/.editorconfig \".editorconfig\")                               |                     |                  |\n| [CODENAMES.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CODENAMES.md \"CODENAMES.md\")                                  |   | [CODENAMES.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CODENAMES.md \"CODENAMES.md\")                                  |                     |                  |\n| [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")                |   | [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md \"CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\")                |                     |                  |\n| [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")                         |   | [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md \"CONTRIBUTING.md\")                         |                     |                  |\n| [GOVERNANCE.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md \"GOVERNANCE.md\")                               |   | [GOVERNANCE.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/GOVERNANCE.md \"GOVERNANCE.md\")                               |                     |                  |\n| [README.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")                                           |   | [README.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/README.md \"README.md\")                                           |                     |                  |\n| [generateReleasePlan.mjs](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/generateReleasePlan.mjs \"generateReleasePlan.mjs\") |   | [generateReleasePlan.mjs](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/generateReleasePlan.mjs \"generateReleasePlan.mjs\") |                     |                  |\n| [schedule.json](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.json \"schedule.json\")                               |   | [schedule.json](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.json \"schedule.json\")                               |                     |                  |\n| [schedule.svg](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.svg \"schedule.svg\")                                  |   | [schedule.svg](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.svg \"schedule.svg\")                                  |                     |                  |\n| View all files                                                                                                           |   |                                                                                                                          |                     |                  |\n\n## Repository files navigation\n\n- [README](#)\n- [Code of conduct](#)\n- [Contributing](#)\n- [Security](#)\n\nMore items\n\n# Node.js Release Working Group\n\n[#nodejs-release-working-group](#nodejs-release-working-group)\n\n## Release schedule\n\n[#release-schedule](#release-schedule)\n\n| Release                                                   | Status              | Codename                                                       | Initial Release | Active LTS Start | Maintenance Start | End-of-life |\n|:---------------------------------------------------------:|:-------------------:|:--------------------------------------------------------------:|:---------------:|:----------------:|:-----------------:|:-----------:|\n| [22.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v22.x/) | **Maintenance LTS** | [Jod](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-jod/)         | 2024-04-24      | 2024-10-29       | 2025-10-21        | 2027-04-30  |\n| [24.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v24.x/) | **Active LTS**      | [Krypton](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-krypton/) | 2025-05-06      | 2025-10-28       | 2026-10-20        | 2028-04-30  |\n| [26.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v26.x/) | **Current**         |                                                                | 2026-05-05      | 2026-10-28       | 2027-10-20        | 2029-04-30  |\n\n| Release | Status    | Codename | Alpha Start | Current Start | LTS Start  | End-of-life |\n|:-------:|:---------:|:--------:|:-----------:|:-------------:|:----------:|:-----------:|\n| 27.x    | **Alpha** |          | 2026-10-28  | 2027-04-22    | 2027-10-20 | 2030-04-30  |\n\nDates are subject to change.\n\n[![LTS Schedule](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/raw/main/schedule.svg)](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.svg)\n\nThe Release schedule is available also as a [JSON](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/schedule.json) file.\n\n### Release Phases\n\n[#release-phases](#release-phases)\n\nThere are four phases that a Node.js release can be in: 'Alpha', 'Current', 'Active Long Term Support (LTS)', and 'Maintenance'. Starting with Node.js 27, every release line goes through the 'Alpha' phase before its first 'Current' release, and every release line is promoted to LTS. Those release lines stay in 'Active LTS' for the whole 30 months of Long Term Support and do not go through the 'Maintenance' phase. See the [Evolving the Node.js Release Schedule](https://nodejs.org/en/blog/announcements/evolving-the-nodejs-release-schedule) announcement for details.\n\nRelease lines up to and including Node.js 26 follow the previous schedule: they do not go through the 'Alpha' phase, and odd-numbered release lines were not promoted to LTS - they did not go through the 'Active LTS' or 'Maintenance' phases.\n\n- Alpha - Should incorporate most of the changes that land on `nodejs/node` main branch, including *semver-major* (breaking) changes. Alpha releases (for example, `27.0.0-alpha.0.0.0`) are signed, tagged, and tested through [CITGM](https://github.com/nodejs/citgm), but their API and ABI may change between releases. They are intended for library authors and CI pipelines, not for production use.\n- Current - Should incorporate most of the non-major (non-breaking) changes that land on `nodejs/node` main branch.\n- Active LTS - New features, bug fixes, and updates that have been audited by the Release team and have been determined to be appropriate and stable for the release line.\n- Maintenance (release lines up to Node.js 26 only) - Critical bug fixes and security updates. New features may be added at the discretion of the Release team - typically only in cases where the new feature supports migration to later release lines.\n\nChanges required for critical security and bug fixes may lead to *semver-major* changes landing within a Current or LTS release stream, such situations will be rare and will land as *semver-minor*. Although, those changes should have a revert option included.\n\nThe term 'supported release lines' will be used to refer to all release lines that are not End-of-Life.\n\n### End-of-Life Releases\n\n[#end-of-life-releases](#end-of-life-releases)\n\n| Release                                                   | Status          | Codename                                                         | Initial Release | Active LTS Start | Maintenance LTS Start | End-of-life                                                          |\n|:---------------------------------------------------------:|:---------------:|:----------------------------------------------------------------:|:---------------:|:----------------:|:---------------------:|:--------------------------------------------------------------------:|\n| v0.10.x                                                   | **End-of-Life** | -                                                                | 2013-03-11      | -                | 2015-10-01            | 2016-10-31                                                           |\n| v0.12.x                                                   | **End-of-Life** | -                                                                | 2015-02-06      | -                | 2016-04-01            | 2016-12-31                                                           |\n| [4.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v4.x/)   | **End-of-Life** | [Argon](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-argon/)       | 2015-09-08      | 2015-10-01       | 2017-04-01            | 2018-04-30                                                           |\n| [5.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v5.x/)   | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2015-10-29      | -                |                       | 2016-06-30                                                           |\n| [6.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v6.x/)   | **End-of-Life** | [Boron](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-boron/)       | 2016-04-26      | 2016-10-18       | 2018-04-30            | 2019-04-30                                                           |\n| [7.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v7.x/)   | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2016-10-25      | -                |                       | 2017-06-30                                                           |\n| [8.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v8.x/)   | **End-of-Life** | [Carbon](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-carbon/)     | 2017-05-30      | 2017-10-31       | 2019-01-01            | 2019-12-31                                                           |\n| [9.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v9.x/)   | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2017-10-01      | -                |                       | 2018-06-30                                                           |\n| [10.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v10.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Dubnium](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-dubnium/)   | 2018-04-24      | 2018-10-30       | 2020-05-19            | 2021-04-30                                                           |\n| [11.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v11.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2018-10-23      | -                |                       | 2019-06-01                                                           |\n| [12.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v12.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Erbium](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-erbium/)     | 2019-04-23      | 2019-10-21       | 2020-11-30            | 2022-04-30                                                           |\n| [13.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v13.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2019-10-22      | -                |                       | 2020-06-01                                                           |\n| [14.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v14.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Fermium](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-fermium/)   | 2020-04-21      | 2020-10-27       | 2021-10-19            | 2023-04-30                                                           |\n| [15.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v15.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2020-10-20      | -                |                       | 2021-06-01                                                           |\n| [16.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v16.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Gallium](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-gallium/)   | 2021-04-20      | 2021-10-26       | 2022-10-18            | [2023-09-11](https://nodejs.org/en/blog/announcements/nodejs16-eol/) |\n| [17.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v17.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2021-10-19      | -                |                       | 2022-06-01                                                           |\n| [18.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v18.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Hydrogen](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-hydrogen/) | 2022-04-19      | 2022-10-25       | 2023-10-18            | 2025-04-30                                                           |\n| [19.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v19.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2022-10-18      | -                |                       | 2023-06-01                                                           |\n| [20.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v20.x/) | **End-of-Life** | [Iron](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-iron/)         | 2023-04-18      | 2023-10-24       | 2024-10-22            | 2026-04-30                                                           |\n| [21.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v21.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2023-10-17      | -                | 2024-04-01            | 2024-06-01                                                           |\n| [23.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v23.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2024-10-15      | -                | 2025-04-01            | 2025-06-01                                                           |\n| [25.x](https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v25.x/) | **End-of-Life** |                                                                  | 2025-10-15      | -                | 2026-04-01            | 2026-06-01                                                           |\n\n## Mandate\n\n[#mandate](#mandate)\n\nThe Release working group's purpose is:\n\n- Management/execution of the release and support process for all releases.\n\nIts responsibilities are:\n\n- Define the release process.\n- Define the content of releases.\n- Generate and create releases.\n- Test Releases.\n- Manage the Alpha, Current, and LTS branches including backporting changes to these branches.\n- Define the policy for what gets backported to release streams.\n\nThe Release working group is structured into teams and membership in the working group does not automatically result in membership in these teams. These teams are:\n\n- Releasers team\n- Backporters team\n- CITGM team\n\nThe `releasers` team is entrusted with the secrets and CI access to be able build and sign releases. **Additions to the releasers team must be approved by the TSC following the process outlined in GOVERNANCE.md.**\n\nThe Release team manages the process/content of LTS releases and the required backporting for these releases. Additions to the Release team needs sign off from the rest of the Release team.\n\nThe Canary in the Gold Mine (CITGM) team maintains CITGM as one of the key sanity checks for releases. This team maintains the CITGM repository and works to keep CITGM builds running and passing regularly. This also includes maintaining the CI jobs in collaboration with the Build Working Group.\n\n## Release Plan\n\n[#release-plan](#release-plan)\n\nStarting with Node.js 27, a new release line is branched from `main` once a year, in October, and receives Alpha releases for six months. The first Alpha release of a new release line happens around the same time the previous release line transitions to Long Term Support. Each April, the release line in Alpha gets its first *semver-major* release (for example, `27.0.0`) and enters the 'Current' phase.\n\nEvery release line stays 'Current' for six months, then transitions to Long Term Support in October. The transition to Long Term Support will happen in a *semver-minor* release. Every release line receives 30 months of Long Term Support, for a total of 36 months from its first Current release to End-of-Life.\n\nRelease lines up to and including Node.js 26 follow the previous schedule: new *semver-major* releases were branched from `main` every six months, with even-numbered versions released in April and odd-numbered versions in October. In coordination with a new *odd-numbered* major release, the previous *even-numbered* major version transitioned to Long Term Support. Every even (LTS) major version is actively maintained for 12 months from the date it enters LTS coverage. Following those 12 months of active support, the major version transitions into \"maintenance\" mode for 18 months. Prior to Node.js 12, the active period was 18 months and the maintenance period 12 months.\n\nSee [Releases Phases](#release-phases) for details of which changes are expected to land during each release phase.\n\nThe exact date that a release will be moved to LTS, moved between LTS modes, or deprecated will be chosen no later than the first day of the month it is to change. If the release team plans to change the release date, it will be done with no less than 14 days notice.\n\nAll LTS releases will be assigned a codename. A list of expected upcoming codenames is available in [CODENAMES.md](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/blob/main/CODENAMES.md).\n\n### LTS Staging Branches\n\n[#lts-staging-branches](#lts-staging-branches)\n\nEvery LTS major version has two branches in the GitHub repository: a release branch and a staging branch. The release branch is used to cut new releases. Only members of the @nodejs/releasers team should land commits onto release branches. The staging branch is used to land cherry-picked or backported commits from main that need to be included in a future release. Only members of @nodejs/backporters should land commits onto staging branches.\n\nFor example, for Node.js v4, there is a `v4.x` branch and a `v4.x-staging` branch. When commits land in main that must be cherry-picked for a future Node.js v4 release, those must be landed into the `v4.x-staging` branch. When commits are backported for a future Node.js v4 release, those must come in the form of pull requests opened against the `v4.x-staging` branch. **Commits are only landed in the `v4.x` branch when a new `v4.x` release is being prepared.**\n\nGenerally, changes are expected to live in an *Alpha* or *Current* release for at least 2 weeks before being backported. It is possible for a commit to land earlier at the discretion of the Release working group.\n\nThe working group members are the union of the Releasers, Backporters and CITGM team members listed below.\n\n### Backporters team\n\n[#backporters-team](#backporters-team)\n\n- [@aduh95](https://github.com/aduh95) - Antoine du Hamel\n- [@BethGriggs](https://github.com/BethGriggs) - Beth Griggs\n- [@codebytere](https://github.com/codebytere) - Shelley Vohr\n- [@guybedford](https://github.com/guybedford) - Guy Bedford\n- [@RafaelGSS](https://github.com/RafaelGSS) - Rafael Gonzaga\n- [@richardlau](https://github.com/richardlau) - Richard Lau\n- [@sxa](https://github.com/sxa) - Stewart X Addison\n\n## Releasers team\n\n[#releasers-team](#releasers-team)\n\n- [@aduh95](https://github.com/aduh95) - Antoine du Hamel\n- [@juanarbol](https://github.com/juanarbol) - Juan José\n- [@marco-ippolito](https://github.com/marco-ippolito) - Marco Ippolito\n- [@RafaelGSS](https://github.com/RafaelGSS) - Rafael Gonzaga\n- [@richardlau](https://github.com/richardlau) - Richard Lau\n- [@ruyadorno](https://github.com/ruyadorno) - Ruy Adorno\n- [@sxa](https://github.com/sxa) - Stewart X Addison\n- [@UlisesGascon](https://github.com/UlisesGascon) - Ulises Gascón\n\n## CITGM team\n\n[#citgm-team](#citgm-team)\n\n- [https://github.com/nodejs/citgm#citgm-team](https://github.com/nodejs/citgm#citgm-team)\n\n## Emeritus\n\n[#emeritus](#emeritus)\n\n### LTS team\n\n[#lts-team](#lts-team)\n\n- [@addaleax](https://github.com/addaleax) - Anna Henningsen\n- [@BethGriggs](https://github.com/BethGriggs) - Bethany Griggs\n- [@bnoordhuis](https://github.com/bnoordhuis) - Ben Noordhuis\n- [@danielleadams](https://github.com/danielleadams) - Danielle Adams\n- [@ErisDS](https://github.com/ErisDS) - Hannah Wolfe\n- [@Fishrock123](https://github.com/Fishrock123) - Jeremiah Senkpiel\n- [@geek](https://github.com/geek) - Wyatt Preul\n- [@gibfahn](https://github.com/gibfahn) - Gibson Fahnestock\n- [@jasnell](https://github.com/jasnell) - James M Snell\n- [@mhdawson](https://github.com/mhdawson) - Michael Dawson\n- [@MylesBorins](https://github.com/MylesBorins) - Myles Borins\n- [@othiym23](https://github.com/othiym23) - Forrest L Norvell\n- [@rvagg](https://github.com/rvagg) - Rod Vagg\n- [@sam-github](https://github.com/sam-github) - Sam Roberts\n- [@shigeki](https://github.com/shigeki) - Shigeki Ohtsu\n- [@srl295](https://github.com/srl295) - Steven R. Loomis\n- [@trevnorris](https://github.com/trevnorris) - Trevor Norris\n- [@yunong](https://github.com/yunong) - Yunong Xiao\n\n### Releasers team\n\n[#releasers-team-1](#releasers-team-1)\n\n- [@bengl](https://github.com/bengl) - Bryan English\n- [@BethGriggs](https://github.com/BethGriggs) - Bethany Griggs\n- [@BridgeAR](https://github.com/BridgeAR) - Ruben Bridgewater\n- [@cjihrig](https://github.com/cjihrig) - Colin Ihrig\n- [@codebytere](https://github.com/codebytere) - Shelley Vohr\n- [@danielleadams](https://github.com/danielleadams) - Danielle Adams\n- [@evanlucas](https://github.com/evanlucas) - Evan Lucas\n- [@Fishrock123](https://github.com/Fishrock123) - Jeremiah Senkpiel\n- [@gibfahn](https://github.com/gibfahn) - Gibson Fahnestock\n- [@jasnell](https://github.com/jasnell) - James M Snell\n- [@MylesBorins](https://github.com/MylesBorins) - Myles Borins\n- [@targos](https://github.com/targos) - Michaël Zasso\n- [@rvagg](https://github.com/rvagg) - Rod Vagg\n\n## About\n\nNode.js Release Working Group\n\n### Topics\n\n[node](https://github.com/topics/node)[nodejs](https://github.com/topics/nodejs)\n\n### Resources\n\n[Readme](#readme-ov-file)\n\n### Code of conduct\n\n[Code of conduct](https://github.com/nodejs/release#coc-ov-file)\n\n### Contributing\n\n[Contributing](#contributing-ov-file)\n\n### Security policy\n\n[Security policy](#security-ov-file)\n\n[Activity](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/activity)\n\n[Custom properties](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/custom-properties)\n\n### Stars\n\n**4.4k** stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n**313** watching\n\n### Forks\n\n[**682** forks](https://github.com/nodejs/Release/forks)\n\n[Report repository](https://github.com/contact/report-content?content_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fnodejs%2FRelease&report=nodejs%20%28user%29)\n\n## Sponsor this project\n\n## Used by\n\n## Contributors\n\n## Languages\n\n## Footer\n\n[https://github.com](https://github.com) © 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n\n### Footer navigation\n\n- [Terms](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service)\n- [Privacy](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement)\n- [Security](https://github.com/security)\n- [Status](https://www.githubstatus.com/)\n- [Community](https://github.community/)\n- [Docs](https://docs.github.com/)\n- [Contact](https://support.github.com?tags=dotcom-footer)\n- Manage cookies\n- Do not share my personal information"},"title":"GitHub - nodejs/Release: Node.js Release Working Group","citations":{"enabled":true}}},"caller":{"type":"code_execution_20260120","tool_id":"srvtoolu_0184JhBH3ntRU6CYoRfsQnxW"}}           }

